# **Line ending normalization (`2026-06-15`).**
#
# Per `agent/memory.md §6` "the pre-existing Windows-side
# `_linux_submodule_backup/` ... mostly CRLF/LF ghosts" — Git
# for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which would
# silently CRLF-convert `.sh` / `.ps1` / CMake sources checked
# out on Windows hosts and break bash strict-mode parsing or
# CMake's `if (DEFINED ...)` matching. Explicitly normalize
# line endings per file class so any Git client on any OS
# (Windows / macOS / Linux) checks out identical byte content.
#
# **Why text=auto vs explicit eol=lf on `*`?**
# `* text=auto` lets Git pick a sensible default per content
# (binary stays binary); the per-extension `text eol=lf` rules
# then override for files we know must be LF on disk. Files
# without an explicit rule (e.g. an operator-authored `.dat`
# file checked in) get Git's auto-detection — binary files stay
# binary, unknown text files default to LF on checkout.
#
# **CRLF on Windows-native build artifacts:**
# `.sln` / `.vcxproj` / `.bat` / `.cmd` are written by Visual
# Studio with CRLF and CRLF is the canonical form on Windows,
# so we explicitly mark them as such. Without this rule, a
# Windows contributor who adds a new `.vcxproj` would
# accidentally commit it with LF endings and Visual Studio
# would either re-write the line endings (producing noisy
# diffs) or fail to load the project.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Shell / PowerShell — LF on disk on every OS.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.ps1           text eol=lf

# CMake / Ninja — LF (CMake docs explicitly say "use Unix
# line endings" for portability; Ninja and clang-cl accept
# both but LF avoids CRLF noise in diff output).
CMakeLists.txt  text eol=lf
*.cmake         text eol=lf
*.cmake.in      text eol=lf

# C / C++ / GLSL / SPIR-V / headers / modules — LF.
*.c             text eol=lf
*.cc            text eol=lf
*.cpp           text eol=lf
*.cxx           text eol=lf
*.h             text eol=lf
*.hh            text eol=lf
*.hpp           text eol=lf
*.hxx           text eol=lf
*.inc           text eol=lf
*.inl           text eol=lf
*.ixx           text eol=lf
*.cppm          text eol=lf
*.vert          text eol=lf
*.frag          text eol=lf
*.geom          text eol=lf
*.comp          text eol=lf
*.tesc          text eol=lf
*.tese          text eol=lf
*.mesh          text eol=lf
